  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::VirtualScienceLab.InteractableObject
  _equipmentName: Compound Light Microscope
  _description: A compound light microscope uses an objective lens and an eyepiece
    to magnify small specimens such as cells. Total magnification is the objective
    magnification multiplied by the eyepiece magnification. Start with the lowest-power
    objective, use coarse focus first, then fine focus. Carry the microscope with
    one hand on the arm and one supporting the base.
